issue_context.body:
OSSL_DESERIALIZER_from_bio fails for file bios (e.g. bio created with BIO_new_file).

The reason is here:
deserializer_lib.c
function deser_process
```
        if (loc == 0) {
            if (BIO_reset(bio) <= 0)
                goto end;
        } else {
```

BIO_reset returns 0 for a file bio. From the documentation:
https://www.openssl.org/docs/man1.0.2/man3/BIO_reset.html
```
BIO_reset() normally returns 1 for success and 0 or -1 for failure. File
BIOs are an exception, they return 0 for success and -1 for failure.
```

The solution, while not very elegant, is to ignore the result of BIO_reset like this is done in other places:
(void)BIO_reset(bio);
